 ## Overview
-The Fragment List-Based Rendering Pipeline is a multi-pass architecture designed for real-time smoke volume rendering that processes geometry through four distinct stages to store and evaluate per-pixel fragment data [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen specifically to maintain high accuracy and circumvent the self-intersection and global intersection problems inherent in raytracing approaches [S1, unofficial]. Unlike the [Volume Rendering Pipeline](1318-volume-rendering-pipeline.md), which typically processes voxels or rays directly, this method rasterizes primitives into fragment lists for deferred evaluation [S1, unofficial].
+The Fragment List-Based Rendering Pipeline is a multi-pass architecture designed for accurate real-time volume rendering of smoke, specifically chosen to circumvent the self-intersection and global intersection artifacts inherent in raytracing approaches [S1, unofficial]. It separates the rendering process into four distinct stages—Clear, Construction, Insertion, and Evaluation—using fragment lists to store and evaluate per-pixel data [S1, unofficial]. Unlike the [Volume Rendering Pipeline](1318-volume-rendering-pipeline.md) which often integrates shading and compositing, or the [Deferred Rendering Pipeline](10584-deferred-rendering-pipeline.md) which relies on G-buffers for geometry, this pipeline explicitly manages fragment accumulation in intermediate storage structures to maintain visual accuracy for participating media [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The pipeline consists of four sequential stages executed by three shader programs: Clear, Render (combining Construction and Insertion), and Display (Evaluation) [S1, unofficial].
+The pipeline executes four sequential stages using three shader programs: Clear, Render (combining Construction and Insertion), and Display (Evaluation) [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** Smoke volume geometry (triangles), vertex attributes (density, flow tangents), and OpenGL buffer objects for storage.
-*   **Output:** Final rendered image with per-pixel visualization of smoke properties.
